{
  "_": "PIN — the MANIFEST of drawing-set.test.mjs's checks, by NAME (R23).",
  "why_a_manifest_and_not_a_count": [
    "SG5 pinned this file's check COUNT (BASELINE_DRAWING_SET = 329, retired with this change).",
    "A count is a scalar over a set: it cannot tell a check that VANISHED from a",
    "check that was ADDED somewhere else. Measured over 46908c6..49502e5, that is",
    "not hypothetical — 29 named checks disappeared in FOUR events, every one of",
    "them masked by a larger increase, and the pin was green throughout."
  ],
  "provenance": {
    "re_derived_by": "i6 VERIFIER backlog round, off integration b9ec338",
    "method": [
      "drawing-set.test.mjs is byte-identical at all seven bisect commits",
      "(md5 7e2e10ff1d5dd2aac9c771ede5e24c12), so every count change came from the",
      "system under test and none from the test. Each commit was checked out into a",
      "disposable worktree, `ok` was instrumented to record every message (they are",
      "template literals evaluated eagerly at the call site, so recording them on",
      "success changes nothing), and the per-commit manifests were diffed.",
      "Each run's instrumented manifest length was reconciled against the count that",
      "same run printed. All seven reconciled exactly."
    ],
    "the_ledger_bisect_table_is_CONFIRMED": "all six rows reproduce (322/353/334/328/327/339).",
    "but_its_arithmetic_is_NOT": [
      "The ledger recorded '26 checks lost in three events'. That summed NET deltas.",
      "Measured by name: 19 + 7 + 1 = 27 lost across those three steps (the middle",
      "step's -6 is 7 lost against 1 added), plus a FOURTH event the ledger records",
      "as a clean +12 which is really 14 added against 2 lost. 29 checks vanished."
    ],
    "the_64_commit_false_pass_window": [
      "The fixture went RED at a6c37f5, one commit BEFORE the ground ruling 7e394eb.",
      "So SG5's 'drawing-set.test.mjs passes' assertion was FALSE for 64 commits and",
      "its count assertion wrong for all 73 — the pin read 283 where 46908c6 already",
      "ran 322. Nobody looked, because the fixture was in no board's population (R12)."
    ],
    "the_plus_39_outside_SG5s_own_stated_window": [
      "SG5's retired comment decomposed +56 of growth across the window it named.",
      "The measured legs inside that window sum to +17, not +56. The other +39",
      "accumulated BEFORE the window the comment named: the decomposition inferred",
      "its own window and inferred it wrong."
    ]
  },
  "the_29_losses_disposed": {
    "RECOVERED (7)": [
      "rooms/dwg/A.01/OPEN WORKSPACE (11)/{area-line,drawn-once,leader}",
      "rooms/dwg/A.02/OPEN WORKSPACE (11)/{area-line,drawn-once,leader}",
      "rooms/dwg/A.02/OPEN WORKSPACE (8)/leader",
      "Present in the pin below. CAVEAT, stated because the name cannot settle it:",
      "the display ordinal is re-derived per render among rooms sharing a base name,",
      "and dwg held 11 / 10 / 12 Open Workspaces across the window — so this is the",
      "same printed identity, not provably the same physical zone."
    ],
    "RETIRED — the isGroundZone fold, ruling 7e394eb (30)": [
      "18 x rooms/dwg/A.0{1,2}/UNASSIGNED (1..6)/{area-line,leader}",
      "12 x rooms/dwg/A.0{1,2}/UNASSIGNED (1..6)/drawn-once",
      "Unassigned is GROUND. The sheets correctly neither schedule nor label ground",
      "zones, so these checks demanded output the product must not produce. The 12",
      "drawn-once ones outlived the ruling as permanent REDS until checkRoomLabels",
      "learned to filter groundZoneTypes() out of its population. Zero UNASSIGNED",
      "checks remain today, and that is the correct number."
    ],
    "RETIRED — the sheet does not exist (1)": [
      "baseline/dwg/sheet-13/row-present. Dropping 6 ground rooms from A.02's",
      "schedule cost the dwg set its 13th (continuation) sheet. Verified: today's",
      "dwg manifest runs sheet-1..12. A baseline row for a sheet that is not",
      "rendered is not an obligation."
    ],
    "RETIRED — conditional assertion, the product improved (4)": [
      "rooms/dwg/A.02/CORE 1/leader",
      "rooms/dwg/A.02/OPEN WORKSPACE (7)/leader",
      "rooms/seeded/A.02/WELLNESS ROOM/leader",
      "(and rooms/dwg/A.02/OPEN WORKSPACE (8)/leader, which then came back)",
      "A leader is only asserted for a label DISPLACED off its room (gap >= 0); a",
      "label sitting on its own footprint owes none. These vanished because the",
      "labels reattached. Each of those rooms KEEPS its drawn-once and area-line",
      "checks — verified present in the pin — so no room lost cover.",
      "THIS IS THE DISTINCTION A COUNT CANNOT DRAW: a check that vanished because an",
      "assertion was deleted and a check that vanished because the product stopped",
      "needing it subtract identically from a scalar. The manifest names which."
    ]
  },
  "contract": [
    "STRICT SET EQUALITY, both directions. A missing name is a defect (coverage",
    "silently left). An unexpected name is a defect too (coverage arrived",
    "unexamined) — the same contract the count had, and the reason a growth event",
    "must be re-pinned deliberately rather than absorbed."
  ],
